        "BIO": "Dr. Bozhou Zhuang is an Assistant Professor in Civil Engineering at UTRGV, where he leads the Structures and Computational Intelligence (SCI) Lab. Prior to joining UTRGV, he spent one year as a Postdoctoral Scholar at University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA) and another year at Georgia Institute of Technology (GT). He received his Ph.D. in Civil Engineering from the University of Southern California (USC) in 2024 and worked as an Intern at Pacific Northwest National Laboratory (PNNL).<br><br>Dr. Zhuang conducts research on intelligent infrastructure systems that can sense their environment, interpret complex data, and support autonomous engineering decisions. Positioned at the convergence of structural engineering and artificial intelligence (AI), his research combines satellite imagery, LiDAR, structural sensing, machine learning (ML), large language models (LLMs), vision-language models (VLMs), and cyber-physical twins. His long-term vision is to transform infrastructure from passive physical assets into adaptive, data-aware systems capable of continuous monitoring, diagnosis, and resilience-informed decision-making.<br><br>For more information, please visit SCI Lab at https://sites.google.com/usc.edu/bozhouzhuang/home.",
